{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgmL1bdpc26qmLz7Lr3oi", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Almost certainly not. Nothing in the job has told anyone:\n\n- **The nightly run crashed before it could alert.** It failed at `os.makedirs(cfg.findings_dir)` in `pipeline/review.py`. That line runs before the findings file is written and before `notify.send` is ever called, so no alerts were queued. The log ends with \"FAILED, nothing published.\"\n- **My test runs didn't alert anyone either.** They wrote to a temporary folder that was deleted afterwards, not to `spool/outgoing/`. There's no `spool/` folder in the repo at all, so nothing is waiting for the relay to deliver.\n\nThere are limits to what I can see. The nightly ran on a separate runner (`/home/runner/work/evalgen`), and I can't check its spool or the relay's delivery history. Going by the code, though, nothing could have been queued there. I also can't tell whether someone found the overspend another way, like a billing dashboard or by reading the failure log.\n\nSo as far as the job goes, finance on-call doesn't know that the `expand` step spent $412.30 against its $250 budget. The policy is meant to prevent exactly that, which is another reason to settle one of the options above soon."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "1e7db960-b5a6-45f3-a021-d6eef8908d54", "uuid": "74ca9661-243d-41ac-9d18-37f419a970f1", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T08:05:25.459Z", "request_id": "req_011CgmL1bMSo2VKzXE8Bm4b7"}
